# rdf:XMLLiteral: the datatype IRI matches, so the answer turns on well-formedness,
# and RDF 1.1 says that lexical space is the strings that are well-balanced,
# self-contained XML content. Deciding that needs an XML parser. It must decline.
<http://ex.org/S> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#NodeShape> .
<http://ex.org/S> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#targetNode> <http://ex.org/alice> .
<http://ex.org/S> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property> <http://ex.org/NoteShape> .
<http://ex.org/NoteShape> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path> <http://ex.org/note> .
<http://ex.org/NoteShape> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#datatype> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#XMLLiteral> .
